sec.p:
The standard lead ECG was monitored continuously at a paper speed of 25 mm/s and an amplification of 0.1 mV/mm. Heart rate was calculated from three RR intervals preceding the measured QT intervals. The QT intervals were measured manually from the onset of the QRS complexes to the end of the T wave and corrected for the patient’s heart rate using Bazett’s formula \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ \mathrm{Q}\mathrm{T}\mathrm{c} = \mathrm{Q}\mathrm{T}/\sqrt{\mathrm{RR}} $$\end{document}QTc=QT/RR. The QTc interval was measured pre-operatively and 10 min after each patient arrived in the PACU.
